v-space: 754M + 420M + 168M = 1.34B (for norm + output)\n# \n# C-space is way worse. v-space is correct.\n\n# === NEW IDEA: Can we avoid computing pmix@G entirely? ===\n# We need ||m|| = ||(1-beta)*u0 + beta*u1||\n# = sqrt((1-beta)''^2*||u0||''^2 + beta''^2*||u1||''^2 + 2*beta*(1-beta)*u0.u1)\n# \n# We know ||u1||''^2 from p1@G.\n# We need ||u0||''^2 and u0.u1.\n# ||u0||''^2 = (p0 * (p0@G)).sum(dim=-1) -> needs p0@G\n# u0.u1 = (p0 * (p1@G)).sum(dim=-1) -> needs p1@G (which we have!)\n# \n# So we need p0@G for ||u0||''^2. That'\"'s another p@G matmul.\n# Total: p1@G + p0@G = 2 matmuls, same as p1@G + pmix@G.\n# \n# Unless... what if ||u0|| can be computed differently?\n# u0 = p0 @ x -> norm is ||p0 @ x||\n# But p0 is softmax of qk\"'^T / sqrt(D), which we already computed.\n# No shortcut there.\n\n# === IDEA: What about using the fact that G = x @ x''^T is symmetric? ===\n# Doesn'\"'t help with matmul speed directly.\n\n# Let me try: what if we reshape p from (B,H,L,L) to (B*H, L, L) \n# and G from (B,L,L) to (B*H, L, L) (by repeating), then do bmm?\n# We saw it's slightly slower. \n\n# === IDEA: Can we use float64 for Gram to accumulate more accurately? ===\n# No, that would be slower and we don't need it.\n\n# === Let me look at the projection more carefully ===\n# Current: (xr @ w.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n# This gives BH L D contiguous.\n# \n# What if we instead do:\n# out = xr @ w.reshape(HD, C).T  # (B*L, H*D) \n# This is laid out as row-major: for each token, we have all heads' dims interleaved\n# Actually no: w.reshape(HD, C) is H*D rows (each a C-dim vector), laid out as head 0 dim 0..D-1, head 1 dim 0..D-1, etc.\n# So the output (B*L, H*D) has columns ordered as: h0d0, h0d1, ..., h0d(D-1), h1d0, ..., h(H-1)d(D-1)\n# \n# When we reshape to (B, L, H, D), the fast axis is D (within a head).\n# Permuting to (B, H, L, D) makes the layout: batch, head, length, dim.\n# \n# Is there a way to avoid the permute? \n# What if q/k/v are in (B, L, H, D) layout and we compute attention differently?\n# q: (B, L, H, D), k: (B, L, H, D)\n# q @ k\"'^T per head: for each head h, q[:, :, h, :] @ k[:, :, h, :].T\n# Result per head: (B, L, L), so total (B, H, L, L)\n# \n# Let'\"'s see: torch.einsum('blhd,bkhd->bhlk', q, k)\n# vs current: q_bhld @ k_bhld.transpose(-1,-2)\n\nq_blhd = (xr @ wq.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D)  # no permute\nk_blhd = (xr @ wk.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D)\nprint(f'q_blhd contiguous: {q_blhd.is_contiguous()}')\n\nq_bhld = q_blhd.permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\nk_bhld = k_blhd.permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n\nbench('q_bhld @ k_bhld.T', lambda: q_bhld @ k_bhld.transpose(-1, -2))\nbench('einsum blhd,bkhd->bhlk', lambda: torch.einsum('blhd,bkhd->bhlk', q_blhd, k_blhd))\n\n# Output of both should be (B, H, L, L) - check if einsum output is contiguous\nout_ein = torch.einsum('blhd,bkhd->bhlk', q_blhd, k_blhd)\nout_matmul = q_bhld @ k_bhld.transpose(-1, -2)\nprint(f'einsum output contiguous: {out_ein.is_contiguous()}')\nprint(f'matmul output contiguous: {out_matmul.is_contiguous()}')\nprint(f'einsum == matmul: {(out_ein - out_matmul).abs().max():.2e}')\n\nprint()\n# And for p @ v:\nv_blhd = (xr @ wv.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D)\nv_bhld = v_blhd.permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\np = torch.randn(B, H, L, L)\n\nbench('p @ v_bhld', lambda: p @ v_bhld)\nbench('einsum bhlk,bkhd->blhd', lambda: torch.einsum('bhlk,bkhd->blhd', p, v_blhd))\n\\\"\n\"","aggregated_output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 108, in <module>\nNameError: name 'xr' is not defined. Did you mean: 'x'?\np @ x_exp (BHL L @ B1L C): 76.802 ms\np @ v (BHLL @ BHLD): 2.848 ms\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
